      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The original courthouse, completed in 1908 for $75,000, now serves as Council Chambers after careful restoration.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6,
        16
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia",
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wetaskiwin",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Wetaskiwin’s first school opened in 1894 and the first newspaper, the Free Lance, began in 1897, marking early community growth.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5,
        25
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia",
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wetaskiwin",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The Reynolds‑Alberta Museum, housed in the former Wetaskiwin airport, preserves the region’s aviation history and the town’s connection to the railway.",
